entry.summary:
Introduction
When I was creating a required input form using React Hook Form and Chakra UI, When testing required fields with React Hook Form + Chakra UI, Unable to find an element with the text: ID is required
The element was displayed correctly in the UI, but not in the test. I used findByText from the Testing Library to wait until the element was found. This fails. expect(screen.getByText("ID is required")).toBeInTheDocument();
Succeeds with asynchronous support. expect(await screen.findByText("ID is required")).toBeInTheDocument();
This resolves the discrepancy where the test fails but the UI shows it. When the UI and Jest behavior differ, suspect asynchronous behavior.
